  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When I launch VRChat, it sometimes fails with an Anti-cheat Error message.\n\nUsually it can be launched correctly to restart VRChat even if this message appears.\n\nBut it can also occur repeatedly and I have to restart every time, it's annoying.\n\nI tried verifying the game file on Steam or reinstalling VRChat, it looks improved the first time, but it also happens again after a while.\n\n(To begin with, this error happens sometimes, not often).\n\nOf course, I've never used any modded clients or any third-party software that interferes with VRChat's process.\n\n(I usually use OVR Advanced Settings, but this error shows up before it starts)\n\nAnd this error also shows the file name that mismatched but these file names are different every time, there are different type like .dll, .vrca, .json, etc...\n\nSo I think VRChat's file verification process has some problems or wrong implementation.\n\nOr rather, what is the \"file version\"?",
